{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly_subpercent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly_subpercent","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L118-L139","doc":"**Six-term per-derivation weights — sub-percent accuracy.**\n\nNames (pattern C of the vacuity-fix playbook) the conditional\nconjecture that, across the proton..⁹Be spectrum (`A = Z + N ≤ 9`),\nthe per-derivation assembly recovers the AME atomic mass to within\nthe empirical max relative error `0.0053` (= 0.53 %, from the\n`A ≤ 9` sweep).  This is a *proposition* — honestly named, not a\nvacuous `: True := trivial`: the mass data live on\n`[SixTermAssemblyData]`, and an instance discharging the bound is\nthe open empirical claim (none = honest open state).\n\nThis `Prop` is the comparison boundary of\n`conj:six-term-per-derivation-weights`: `measured_mass` is AME data and\n`0.0053` is a measured error, so nothing here is a formal consequence of the\nassembly `binding_assembly`, which takes every energy scale as a parameter.\n\nRef: paper_six_term_isotope_sweep.py (assemble_per_derivation_weights)\nRef: docs/audits/2026-05-04-per-derivation-weights-result.md ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.measured_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.measured_pos","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L116-L116","doc":"Measured masses are positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.measured_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.measured_mass","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L114-L114","doc":"The measured AME atomic mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.assembled_mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.assembled_mass","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L112-L112","doc":"The per-derivation assembled atomic mass (MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.SixTermAssemblyData","kind":"class","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L104-L116","doc":"The genuinely-open empirical inputs for the sub-percent\naccuracy claim: for an isotope `(Z, N)`, the per-derivation\nassembled atomic mass `assembled_mass` and the measured AME\natomic mass `measured_mass` (both in MeV, `measured_mass > 0`).\nA categorical derivation of these from the substrate is open;\nthey are carried as hypotheses (pattern C), not asserted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.not_binding_assembly_of_free_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.not_binding_assembly_of_free_data","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The assembly is refutable at freely-chosen data**, which is why it is\nnamed rather than carried as a `sorry`.\n\nWith every term zero it reads `1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly_eq_zero_of_no_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly_eq_zero_of_no_separation","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L58-L74","doc":"**No binding when free and bound agree** — derived.\n\nIf every per-term value coincides between the free and atomic\nconfigurations and the chirality coefficient is `a_K = 1`, the assembly\ngives `B = 0`.  Each of the five terms is a difference that vanishes, the\nfourth through its `(a_K − 1)` factor.\n\nThe sanity check the assembly must pass to be a *binding* energy at all, and\nthe reason the shape is worth naming: it is a hypothesis something is proved\nfrom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SixTermPerDerivationWeights.binding_assembly","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SixTermPerDerivationWeights.lean#L31-L56","doc":"**The six-term binding-energy assembly**\n([`conj:six-term-per-derivation-weights`](../../../mass-theory/six-term-per-derivation-weights.md)),\nas a proposition over caller-supplied data:\n\n      B = E_0_β · (T1_free − T1_atom)\n        + α · (T23_atom − T23_free)\n        + m_e · (T4_atom − T4_free)\n        + E_0_β · (a_K − 1) · T1_atom\n        + (T6_atom − T6_free)\n\n**Named, not asserted.**  This is the declaration the block's `lean.ref`\nactually resolves to — see the note below on what it replaced.\n\nNothing here constructs the descended Markov trace `T1`, the `Φ_q` vertex\nterms `T2`/`T3`, `τ(C_dim_q)` (`T4`), the cyclotomic residue sum `T6`, the\nchirality coefficient `a_K`, or the Borromean–Catalan scale `α = m_e·8G`;\nthey are reals the caller supplies.  So this states which quantities are\ncombined and how, not why they are the ones that appear. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:six-term-per-derivation-weights","label":"conj:six-term-per-derivation-weights","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/six-term-per-derivation-weights.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}